  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “Sunday within the Octave of the Nativity of the Lord” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: As long as the heir is a child, he differeth nothing from a servant, though he be lord of all; but he is under tutors and governors until the time appointed by the father. So we also, when we were children, were serving under the elements of the world. But when the fullness of time was come, God sent His Son, made of a woman, made under the Law, that He might redeem those who were under the Law, that we might receive the adoption of sons. And because ye are sons, God hath sent the Spirit of His Son into your hearts, crying: Abba, Father. Therefore he is now no more a servant, but a son; and if a son, then an heir through God.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w045", "w046"], "anchor": "w045", "gloss": "His Son" }] }
  },
